    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1010">

                <pb facs="1508" n="1482" xml:id="pg1482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/7–2054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-20T21:00:00+01:00">July 20, 1954—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 692. Following declarations of French Government have been agreed to by all
                    parties: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Declaration of the Government of the French Republic (reference: Article
                            10 of the final act<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1010-f1"/>).</p>
                        <p>“The Government of the French Republic declares that it is prepared to
                            withdraw its troops from the territories of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam
                            at the request of the governments concerned and in periods which will be
                            fixed in agreement with those governments, with the exception of those
                            cases where, by agreement of the two parties, a certain number of French
                            troops may be left at fixed points and for fixed periods.”</p>
                        <p>“Declaration of the Government of the French Republic (reference: Article
                            11 of the final act).</p>
                        <p>“In the settling of all the problems related to the restoration and the
                            strengthening of peace in Cambodia, Laos, and Vietnam, the Government of
                            the French Republic will base itself upon respect for the independence
                            and the sovereignty, the unity and the territorial integrity of
                            Cambodia, of Laos and of Vietnam.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1010-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1010-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the draft final declaration (or act), see telegrams Secto 684 and
                    Secto 690, July 20, <ref target="#pg1474">pp. 1474</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg1480">1480</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
